 over me\nWay too high to simmer down, might as well overheat\nToo close to comfort as blood rush my favorite vein\nHeartbeat racin' like junkie's, I just need you to want me\n\n[bridge]\nI askin' too much? Let me put the head in\nOoh, I don't want more than that. Girl, I respect the cat\nI promise just touch. Let me put the head in\n\"It's okay,\" she said, \"It's okay.\"\n\n[bridge]\nI wake in the mornin', my head spinnin' from the last night\n\n[bridge]\nManager called, the lobby called, it's 11:30\nDid this before, promised myself I' be hour early\nRoom full of clothes, bag full of money: call it loose change\nFumbled my jewelry, 100k, I lost new chain\nHop on the bird, hit the next city for another M\nN..\nTake me nap and do it again\n\n[bridge]\nWe all woke up, tryna tune to the daily news\nLookin' for confirmation, hopin' election wasn't true\nAll of us worried, all of us buried, and our feeling's deep\nNone of us married to his proposal, make us feel cheap\nStill and sad, distraught and mad, tell the neighbor 'bout it\n\n[bridge]\nTime passin', things change\nRevertin' back to our daily programs, stuck in our ways; drone\n\n[bridge]\nI need some water, somethin' came over me\nWay too high to simmer down, might as well overheat\nToo close to comfort as blood rush my favorite vein\nHeartbeat racin' like junkie's, I just need you to want me\n\n[bridge]\nI askin' too much? Let me put the head in\nOoh, I don't want more than that. Girl, I respect the cat\nI promise just touch. Let me put the head in\n\"It's okay,\" she said, \"It's okay.\"",
